{"kind":"request","text":"Reduce per-record cold audit cost, or let gs verify use a verified checkpoint.","body":{"conditions":"Measured at main 316d5aeb (docs/reference/performance.md): a cold full audit costs 55.4 ms and exactly 2.00 git subprocesses per record, linear to within 0.5% across depths 100/257/500, and 242.3 s with 11,581 git subprocesses for this repository's 5,787 records. That misses the PREVIEW cold-verify target of 5 min at 50,000 records (extrapolates to ~46 min, 9.2x over) and the FIRST-PRODUCTION target of 60 min at 500,000 records (~7.7 h, 7.7x over). Suspected bounding component: two git subprocess spawns per record on the audit path. Satisfied when a cold audit of 50,000 records completes within 5 min on comparable hardware without weakening any verification invariant, with the subprocess-per-record ratio reported.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}